{"id":"coding-debugging","title":"Coding: finding and fixing bugs","subject":"Coding","label":"Coding","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":156,"duration":155.71,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":442,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":15.485},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":15.485,"end":48.075},{"id":"explain2","title":"Debug method","start":48.075,"end":70.995},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":70.995,"end":93.955},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":93.955,"end":102.385},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":102.385,"end":108.145},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":108.145,"end":130.545},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":130.545,"end":155.71}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.35,"text":"Your program runs, but the total looks wrong. Nothing crashed, so what happened?","w":[0.52,0.72,1.24,1.6,1.74,1.9,2.22,2.48,3.44,3.76,4.6,4.76,4.94]},{"s":0,"a":5.8,"b":12.88,"text":"I'm Kora. Debugging is how we find and fix that. Every programmer meets bugs, and today you'll learn a calm method.","w":[5.92,6.12,6.92,7.48,7.62,7.78,7.96,8.28,8.4,8.66,9.46,9.7,10.22,10.46,11.26,11.38,11.8,12.02,12.22,12.3,12.58]},{"s":0,"a":13.18,"b":15.06,"text":"It is normal work, not failure.","w":[13.24,13.36,13.48,13.84,14.42,14.66]},{"s":1,"a":15.91,"b":19.57,"text":"Every programmer writes bugs. A bug is a mistake in your code.","w":[15.96,16.2,16.76,17.06,17.82,17.94,18.24,18.36,18.44,18.94,19.02,19.2]},{"s":1,"a":19.87,"b":24.95,"text":"Debugging means finding it and fixing it. It is normal work, not a sign of failure.","w":[19.87,20.4,20.7,21.14,21.3,21.48,21.88,22.5,22.64,22.8,23.18,23.78,24,24.1,24.38,24.5]},{"s":1,"a":25.25,"b":33.13,"text":"Three kinds of error matter. A syntax error breaks the rules of the language, like a missing colon or bracket. The program will not start.","w":[25.28,25.6,25.9,26.06,26.32,26.92,27.02,27.56,27.84,28.18,28.3,28.56,28.66,28.78,29.46,29.64,29.72,30.06,30.5,30.62,31.62,31.76,32.24,32.46,32.72]},{"s":1,"a":33.43,"b":41.67,"text":"A runtime error happens while the program runs. Dividing by zero, or using a name that does not exist, stops it with an error message.","w":[33.48,33.58,34.12,34.4,34.82,35,35.14,35.62,36.54,37,37.2,38.06,38.26,38.52,38.6,38.86,39,39.2,39.42,40.26,40.64,40.72,40.86,41.02,41.24]},{"s":1,"a":41.97,"b":47.65,"text":"A logic error runs without complaint but gives the wrong answer. It is the hardest kind to spot.","w":[42.02,42.12,42.56,42.86,43.16,43.5,44.24,44.44,44.7,44.82,45.14,45.98,46.08,46.2,46.32,46.76,47.08,47.2]},{"s":2,"a":48.5,"b":52.98,"text":"Start by reading the error message. It tells you the type of error and the line number.","w":[48.6,48.92,49.14,49.44,49.64,49.88,50.76,50.88,51.14,51.26,51.38,51.66,51.88,52.22,52.34,52.46,52.7]},{"s":2,"a":53.28,"b":57.56,"text":"Then reproduce the problem, so you see it happen again. Make the problem smaller.","w":[53.32,53.54,54.04,54.14,54.88,55.06,55.22,55.4,55.5,55.78,56.46,56.66,56.76,57.14]},{"s":2,"a":57.86,"b":63.86,"text":"Print the values of variables to see what is really happening. Change one thing at a time, then test again.","w":[57.86,58.1,58.22,58.66,58.76,59.38,59.54,59.74,59.92,60.06,60.38,61.28,61.74,61.92,62.12,62.24,62.32,62.96,63.18,63.5]},{"s":2,"a":64.16,"b":70.57,"text":"Explain the code aloud line by line. Programmers call this rubber duck debugging. Take a break when you feel stuck.","w":[64.26,64.72,64.86,65.16,65.7,65.98,66.16,66.76,67.36,67.58,67.84,68.16,68.42,69.24,69.48,69.54,69.84,69.96,70.08,70.32]},{"s":3,"a":71.42,"b":79.18,"text":"Suppose your code should average three marks. It says mark one plus mark two plus mark three divided by three, with no brackets.","w":[71.5,71.86,72.06,72.34,72.62,73,73.28,74.22,74.34,74.64,75.04,75.26,75.54,75.82,76.12,76.42,76.68,76.96,77.34,77.52,78.28,78.48,78.64]},{"s":3,"a":79.48,"b":85.74,"text":"So only the third mark is divided by three. The program runs with no complaint, but the average comes out far too high.","w":[79.6,79.82,80.06,80.22,80.52,80.82,80.92,81.3,81.48,81.8,81.92,82.42,82.72,82.98,83.22,83.92,84.04,84.26,84.56,84.8,85.04,85.28,85.46]},{"s":3,"a":86.04,"b":93.53,"text":"Put brackets around the sum before dividing. Now all three marks are added first, then divided by three. The answer is correct.","w":[86.08,86.3,86.7,86.94,87.08,87.38,87.72,88.84,89.16,89.34,89.58,89.84,90,90.24,91.02,91.2,91.6,91.76,92.66,92.84,93.12,93.22]},{"s":4,"a":94.38,"b":99.49,"text":"Your program runs with no error message but prints the wrong total. Which kind of error is it?","w":[94.4,94.62,95.12,95.38,95.64,95.92,96.14,96.52,96.74,97.04,97.16,97.44,98.38,98.6,98.8,98.96,99.24,99.38]},{"s":4,"a":99.94,"b":101.96,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[99.96,100.28,100.5,100.64,100.92,101.46,101.64]},{"s":5,"a":102.81,"b":107.72,"text":"It is a logic error, because the program runs without complaint but gives the wrong answer.","w":[102.88,103,103.12,103.2,103.68,104.3,104.6,104.72,105.24,105.48,105.8,106.58,106.76,107,107.12,107.4]},{"s":6,"a":108.57,"b":114.61,"text":"Common mistake one. Ignoring the error message. Read it first. It often names the problem and the line.","w":[108.64,109,109.48,110.04,110.44,110.6,110.82,111.54,111.74,111.86,112.66,112.86,113.14,113.38,113.48,114,114.12,114.22]},{"s":6,"a":114.91,"b":121.91,"text":"Common mistake two. Changing many things at once. Change one thing, then test, so you know what worked.","w":[114.98,115.38,115.8,116.62,117.08,117.36,117.64,117.86,118.62,119.04,119.24,119.96,120.2,121,121.16,121.26,121.4,121.56]},{"s":6,"a":122.21,"b":130.12,"text":"Common mistake three. Assuming the computer is wrong or never testing simple values. Check small values by hand before you blame the machine.","w":[122.26,122.6,122.98,123.7,124.12,124.24,124.68,124.82,125.24,125.38,125.68,126.06,126.36,127.42,127.68,127.96,128.38,128.54,128.88,129.16,129.3,129.56,129.66]},{"s":7,"a":130.97,"b":140.09,"text":"Recap. Bugs are normal. Syntax errors stop the program starting, runtime errors stop it while running, and logic errors give wrong answers.","w":[131.04,132,132.3,132.44,133.28,133.86,134.34,134.66,134.78,135.18,136.04,136.58,136.88,137.2,137.3,137.52,138.2,138.36,138.78,139.1,139.34,139.68]},{"s":7,"a":140.39,"b":144.55,"text":"Read the error message, reproduce the problem, and change one thing at a time.","w":[140.44,140.66,140.88,141.12,141.76,142.28,142.38,143.06,143.26,143.7,143.84,144.04,144.14,144.22]},{"s":7,"a":144.85,"b":147.57,"text":"Explain your code aloud, and take a break when stuck.","w":[144.9,145.34,145.5,145.76,146.4,146.54,146.78,146.84,147.1,147.32]},{"s":7,"a":147.87,"b":151.31,"text":"Top tip: test with small values you can check by hand.","w":[147.88,148.18,148.9,149.22,149.44,149.78,150.28,150.42,150.56,150.82,151.02]},{"s":7,"a":151.61,"b":155.11,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and you will debug with confidence.","w":[151.62,151.88,152.44,152.62,153.42,153.56,153.7,153.86,154.26,154.42]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Program runs, but total looks wrong"},{"at":5.7,"kind":"term","text":"debugging","detail":"finding and fixing bugs"},{"at":13.08,"kind":"text","text":"Normal work, not failure"}]},{"at":15.66,"heading":"Bugs and debugging","items":[{"at":15.81,"kind":"term","text":"bug","detail":"a mistake in your code"},{"at":19.77,"kind":"term","text":"debugging","detail":"finding a bug and fixing it"},{"at":25.15,"kind":"term","text":"syntax error","detail":"breaks language rules (missing colon/bracket); program won't start"},{"at":33.33,"kind":"term","text":"runtime error","detail":"happens while running; e.g. divide by zero or unknown name stops it"},{"at":41.87,"kind":"term","text":"logic error","detail":"runs without complaint but gives wrong answer; hardest to spot"}]},{"at":48.25,"heading":"Debug method","items":[{"at":48.4,"kind":"term","text":"error message","detail":"tells error type and line number"},{"at":53.18,"kind":"text","text":"Reproduce the problem; make it smaller"},{"at":57.76,"kind":"text","text":"Print variables; change one thing, test again"},{"at":64.06,"kind":"term","text":"rubber duck debugging","detail":"explain code aloud line by line; take a break when stuck"}]},{"at":71.17,"heading":"Worked example: average","items":[{"at":71.32,"kind":"formula","text":"mark1 + mark2 + mark3 / 3"},{"at":79.38,"kind":"text","text":"Runs, but the average is far too high"},{"at":85.94,"kind":"formula","text":"(mark1 + mark2 + mark3) / 3"}]},{"at":93.95,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":93.95,"kind":"question","text":"Your program runs with no error message but prints the wrong total. Which kind of error is it?"}]},{"at":102.56,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":102.71,"kind":"term","text":"logic error","detail":"runs without complaint but gives wrong answer"},{"at":102.71,"kind":"text","text":"Program runs, wrong total → logic error"}]},{"at":108.32,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":108.47,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ignoring the error message"},{"at":114.81,"kind":"wrong","text":"Changing many things at once"},{"at":122.11,"kind":"wrong","text":"Blaming the computer; no simple tests"}]},{"at":130.72,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":130.87,"kind":"text","text":"Bugs normal: syntax, runtime, logic"},{"at":140.29,"kind":"text","text":"Read error, reproduce, change one thing"},{"at":144.75,"kind":"text","text":"Explain code aloud; take a break when stuck"},{"at":147.77,"kind":"tip","text":"Top tip: test with small values you can check by hand"},{"at":151.51,"kind":"text","text":"Keep practising with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":102.21,"seconds":10,"question":"Your program runs with no error message but prints the wrong total. Which kind of error is it?","answer":"A logic error: it runs without complaint but gives the wrong answer."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}